==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{affix|ru|врать|-ач|id2=agent noun}}. Originally meant "witch-doctor, enchanter".

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-врач.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|b|a=an|}}

# {{lb|ru|medicine|formal}} [[therapist]], not [[surgeon]], not [[hospital]] [[nurse]]
# [[doc]], [[vet]], [[medic]], [[physician]], [[doctor]]

====Usage notes====
A female medical doctor is referred to as '''врач''', or [[женщина]]-врач, or, colloquially only, [[врачиха]].

The archaic vocative form {{m|ru|вра́чу}} is currently found only in the set phrase "Вра́чу, исцелися сам" ''(Physician, heal thyself).''

